<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aparajitavarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 885–897</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Aparajita Pallava</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aparajitavarman was the last important king of the Pallava dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>. Around 885, with his Western Ganga ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvipati-i">Prithvipati I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> support, he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varaguna-ii">Varaguna II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sripurambiyam">Battle of Sripurambiyam</a>. Around 897 he was defeated by the Chola king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aditya-i">Aditya I</a>, who annexed the Pallava kingdom.</p></div>
